    },
    {
      "image": "videos/08-great-filter/2.jpg",
      "seconds": 17.43,
      "text": "There are hundreds of billions of stars in our galaxy alone, most with planets. The galaxy is over thirteen billion years old. A single civilization with patience and simple rockets could cross it in a few million years, which is a rounding error on that timescale. So the sky should be crowded with evidence. We look, and we find nothing. Not one signal.",
      "delivery": {
        "rate": 12,
        "pitch": 0
      },
      "clips": [
        {
          "src": "videos/08-great-filter/v2-1.mp3",
